# ec/tools/firmware_regions.py and ec/tools/bank_map_score.py, both wired into
# the cheap gate as one `check_bank_map()`.
#
# Prepared here rather than landed, because `.github/scripts/agent-gates.sh` is
# copied from the agent-pipeline template and the pipeline's push token has no
# `workflow` scope, so a branch editing it fails at the end of the PR rather
# than at the start of it. `docs/agent-pipeline.md` says the same thing about
# every other leg of this a human has to land.
#
# To land it:
#
#   git apply docs/ci/agent-gates-bank-map-score.patch
#
# and that is the whole change.
#
# The placement is the interesting half of this and it is a measurement, not a
# preference. The obvious shape -- two entries in the `for tool in` list and
# one `gate` line -- is not available. The `gate` list is saturated: every
# patch in `docs/ci/` that wants a line takes a three-line context window out
# of it, so cut a one-line patch at every insertion point `git diff` would
# offer one, the way a real patch is cut, and try each against the committed
# set in both orders -- **each one collides with an existing patch and none
# composes**. The `for tool in` list is saturated the same way, which
# is what `ec/tools/check_gate_arm_coverage.py`'s own comment about its tool
# list is warning about. `agent-gates-capture-claims.patch` carries the
# original measurement at `d3304785`; this is the same probe re-run against
# the set as committed now, with the same result.
#
# So this is one `check_bank_map()` function at a free anchor plus one call
# from `check_ghidra_tooling`, which is the function whose own comment calls
# itself "the decompilation pipeline's own self-tests and staleness checks" and
# whose every arm is a `--check` plus a `--self-test` on a tool that needs no
# Ghidra -- which is exactly what these two are. `agent-gates-findings-frozen.
# patch` is the precedent for calling a check from an existing function rather
# than taking a `gate` line, and it took the line at the top of
# `check_doc_links`; this call goes into a different function so the two
# three-line context windows stay disjoint. `tools/test_agent_gates_patches.py`
# proves every ordered pair, and this is the placement that needs no pair.
#
# The checks are cheap-tier by the split in that script's own header: both
# read committed text and `ec/firmware/GMxMGxx_11.800`, and neither needs
# Ghidra, the network or an assembler. The two `--check` arms are not the same
# claim, so it is worth saying what each one refuses rather than leaving
# "reproducible from the committed inputs" to cover both:
# `bank_map_score.py --check` refuses a `calls_stub` row the image does not
# support and a population it cannot reproduce from the image it was handed,
# and `firmware_regions.py --check` fails only on a block whose verdict is
# outside the three its classifier can produce. Neither compares its report
# against a stored one, so a firmware image that has changed under them is not
# what either arm catches.
# `--self-test` is the half that matters, and it is the same half the other
# arms in `check_ghidra_tooling` are there for: it pins the refusals. A census
# that had quietly started calling a block `code`, and a scorer that had
# quietly started calling a pair confirmed, both print every known answer and
# neither is caught without the assertions beside them.
#
# The fixtures that would be worth running from a gate live in
# `ec/tools/testdata/`, and `tools/run-tests.sh` collects both suites on its
# own -- `bash tools/run-tests.sh` is what covers them, not this.
#
diff --git a/.github/scripts/agent-gates.sh b/.github/scripts/agent-gates.sh
index 16c70c3..0000000 100755
@@ -93,6 +93,20 @@
   return "$rc"
 }
 
+# The bank-to-file-offset map the whole decompilation rests on, and the region
+# census the image's layout was never checked against. Both read committed text
+# and the committed firmware -- no Ghidra, no network, no assembler -- which is
+# what puts them in this cheap tier, and both take --check and --self-test and
+# nothing else, so they fit the shape the calls below expect.
+check_bank_map() {
+  local rc=0
+  python3 ec/tools/firmware_regions.py --check || rc=1
+  python3 ec/tools/firmware_regions.py --self-test || rc=1
+  python3 ec/tools/bank_map_score.py --check || rc=1
+  python3 ec/tools/bank_map_score.py --self-test || rc=1
+  return "$rc"
+}
+
 # The decompilation pipeline's own self-tests and staleness checks. Each of
 # these runs with no Ghidra and no network, which is what lets them live in a
 # gate: a full Ghidra rebuild is minutes, and this gate has to stay inside the
@@ -100,6 +114,17 @@
 # opt-in step (build_ec_decompile.py --self-test --oracle).
 check_ghidra_tooling() {
   local rc=0 scratch tool
